{"name":"Fair Orchid","hex":"#bda7be","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fair","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Beautiful, of a pleasing appearance, with a pure and fresh quality.","Unblemished (figuratively or literally); clean and pure; innocent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something which is fair (in various senses of the adjective).","A woman, a member of the ‘fair sex’; also as a collective singular, women."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fair"},{"term":"orchid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the orchid family (Orchidaceae), bearing unusually-shaped flowers of beautiful colours. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A light bluish-red, violet-red or purple colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a light purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fair","blocks":[{"text":"A fair is gathering of people for a variety of entertainment or commercial activities. Fairs are typically temporary with scheduled times lasting from an afternoon to several weeks. Fairs showcase a wide range of goods, products, and services, and often include competitions, exhibitions, and educational activities. Fairs can be thematic, focusing on specific industries or interests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/2008Overview1.JPG/330px-2008Overview1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair","wikidata":"Q288514"},{"title":"Orchid","blocks":[{"text":"Orchids are plants that belong to the family Orchidaceae, a diverse and widespread group of flowering plants with blooms that are often colourful and fragrant. Orchids are cosmopolitan plants, living in diverse habitats on every continent except Antarctica. The world's richest diversity of orchid genera and species is in the tropics. Many species are epiphytes, living on trees. The flowers and their pollination mechanisms are highly specialized, attracting insect pollinators by colour, pattern, scent, pheromones, and sometimes by mimicking female insects. Orchids have very small seeds, relying on fungal partners for germination. Some orchids have no leaves, either photosynthesizing with their roots or relying entirely on fungal partners for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid","wikidata":"Q25308"},{"title":"Orchid (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Orchid is a bright rich purple color that resembles the color which various orchids often exhibit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Labiata.jpg/330px-Labiata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid_(color)","wikidata":"Q1925148"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/500px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/1280px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Fairgames.jpg/500px-Fairgames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A boy at the fish pond, the Rockton World's Fair, harvest festival, Canada, 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFairgames.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg/500px-Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg/500px-Goose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roundabouts (also known as a carousel or merry-go-round) are traditional attractions, often seen at fairs.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoose_Fair_Roundabout.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG/500px-1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG/1280px-1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG/500px-1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Village fair by Flemish artist Gillis Mostaert 1590","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1590_Mostaert_Dorfkirmes_anagoria.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Delaware_State_Fair_2009.jpg/500px-Delaware_State_Fair_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Delaware_State_Fair_2009.jpg/500px-Delaware_State_Fair_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fairs can include exhibitions of animals, and before competitions, the animals will be groomed by their owners.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADelaware_State_Fair_2009.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Rosa_Bonheur%2C_The_Horse_Fair%2C_1852%E2%80%9355.jpg/500px-Rosa_Bonheur%2C_The_Horse_Fair%2C_1852%E2%80%9355.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn